CREATED:20260416T115803Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260416T115803Z
UID:10003640-1778529600-1778535000@nertamid.org
SUMMARY:What Comes Next with Nadav Tamir
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for a timely conversation with Nadav Tamir\, Executive Director of J Street Israel\, former Israeli Consul General to New England\, and senior adviser to President Shimon Peres. Nadav will discuss the region’s most recent developments – including the war with Iran – and reflect on the necessity of diplomatic engagement\, accountability in US foreign policy and other elements of J Street’s vision of the way forward.  \nRegister Here Through J Street!
URL:https://nertamid.org/event/what-comes-next-with-nadav-tamir/
CATEGORIES:General
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Temple Ner Tamid
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260512T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260512T133000
DTSTAMP:20260506T235638
CREATED:20250903T181951Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20250903T181951Z
UID:10002868-1778587200-1778592600@nertamid.org
SUMMARY:Lunch With the Rabbi
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our monthly “Lunch with the Rabbi” class where each year a group of dedicated congregants meet and discuss a provocative Jewish book. This year we will be reading Rabbi Katz’s own Yochanan’s Gamble: Judaism’s Pragmatic Approach to Life. The book makes the claim that rather than have the intractable\, strident discourse of today’s politics\, we need to embrace the pragmatism of the Rabbis\, which began with Yochanan ben Zakkai’s decision to trade Jerusalem of Yavneh. In essence\, we can benefit today from the model of the ancient rabbis who make messy compromises\, lead (but not too far ahead of their flock)\, change laws if they don’t work\, and preserve peace within their community in order to better function in our day of division. \nGoing forward\, the class will meet monthly on the 2nd Tuesday of each month. Brown bag lunch (dairy or pareve) at 12pm\, hybrid learning at 12:30pm. \nREGISTER HERE!
URL:https://nertamid.org/event/lunch-with-the-rabbi-4/2026-05-12/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
END:VEVENT
